# Ripgrep configuration for this repository — loaded through RIPGREP_CONFIG_PATH,
# which .claude/settings.json sets for every session opened here.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS, measured 2026-08-17:
#   `rg -l "NEXT:" .` did not find .planning/research/rival-intel/00-LEDGER.md,
#   a tracked file whose fourth line literally reads "**NEXT: 28**".
#   ripgrep skips dot-directories by default, and THIS PROJECT KEEPS ITS STATE,
#   ITS OPEN-WORK RESEARCH AND ITS RIVAL LEDGER IN `.planning/` AND ITS DOORS IN
#   `.claude/`. So the default made every session's sweep silently blind to the
#   two directories that decide what is true here — including a sweep run to prove
#   a deleted file left no trace anywhere.
#
# The CEO named the risk himself the same evening: "e bunu diğerleri de yaparsa
# opus 5 ler arama yaparken?" — a defect one session works around is a defect
# every later session still walks into. This is the fix at its source.

# Search dot-directories: .planning, .claude, .github are all real content here.
--hidden

# ...but never the git object store, which --hidden would otherwise open.
--glob=!.git/

# Keep matches readable when a line is a 400-character ledger row.
--max-columns=400
--max-columns-preview
